{"title":"2020 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, the perimeter of the triangle is equal to the perimeter of the rectangle.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317f9df19f338457dacf9cff1115dcbc90ad0e52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 11 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 14 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> of a shape is equal to the sum of its side lengths, and for a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a>, this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the sum of the sum of its height and width.\n</p><p>We can see that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a>'s side lengths are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da2038a882b47e2184ab809431639593cff639b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da2038a882b47e2184ab809431639593cff639b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/3/a6369813341b735f6687d5b839077ef58d222ebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> because it is isosceles. Thus, the perimeter of the triangle would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/2/7022010c1a3eefbfbbd7120c711bdc55642448b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\text{ cm} + 12 \\text{ cm} + 14 \\text { cm} = 24 \\text{ cm} + 14 \\text{ cm} = 38 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"387\" height=\"15\" />. This must also be equal to the perimeter of the rectangle, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b6195ad671a3d6b32145665d37355cee2c64b7e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(x + 8) = 38$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/1/9419002afb8debaceb6ac596adc8c599867d593f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 8 = \\frac{38}{2} = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd0717c97ef554367a4e602bcdae2bab2211b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 19 - 8 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"175\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2020 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2020 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_G